/T (Phase-II: In this phase, the BERT-Doc-NER-Max was formulated, by fine-tuning BERT-Doc-NER on the complete dataset of 100 samples instead of the 80:20 split as of Phase-I to enhance pattern generalization and model performance improvements.)
/E (Phase-II: In this phase, the BERT-Doc-NER-Max was formulated, by fine-tuning BERT-Doc-NER on the complete dataset of 100 samples instead of the 80:20 split as of Phase-I to enhance pattern generalization and model performance improvements.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
